---
description: Rules for the Next.js quarantine console.
globs: dashboard/**
alwaysApply: false
---

The dashboard is the surface the demo video films. Two consequences:

1. It renders real data from a running proxy. Never mock, never seed, never
   fake a diff for the screenshot. A judge who spots a mock discards the whole
   submission.
2. The quarantine detail screen — the word-level diff — is the single most
   important screen in the project. It is what a judge pauses on. Legibility at
   1920×1080 without horizontal scrolling is a hard requirement; diff render
   under 100 ms.

Encode seal status in shape as well as colour (pill plus text), never colour
alone. Semantic status colour is separate from the accent hue.

Do not scaffold this before Gate 1 passes. If Gate 2 slips, this whole
directory is cut and replaced with coloured terminal output — build nothing
here that the terminal path would have to reimplement.
